1
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:11,450
[CHECKING HER LOOK JUST A BIT.]

2
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:17,010
[WHAT ARE YOU GUYS EVEN DOING?!]

3
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:25,010
[BRIEFING VERY CLOSELY.]

4
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,370
[DESIGNING THE SCENE A LITTLE.]

5
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:43,570
[WHY ARE YOU STARING AT ‘NONG’ SO MUCH?]

6
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:50,297
[IS THIS STILL A REHEARSAL?]

7
00:00:50,318 --> 00:00:53,734
(The guys, please allow some space.)

8
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:56,450
[CLEARING OFF SPACE.]

9
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:01,610
[GIVING THEM SOME SUPPORT.]

10
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:07,560
So this is how we’re supposed
to be touching, and this is not.

11
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:08,001
[WHATCHA DOIN'?]
So this is how we’re supposed
to be touching, and this is not.

12
00:01:08,001 --> 00:01:09,010
[WHATCHA DOIN'?]

13
00:01:10,453 --> 00:01:13,158
It still feels like one is leading
and one is following.

14
00:01:13,171 --> 00:01:14,648
But when people are in love, it’s like,

15
00:01:14,706 --> 00:01:15,360
“I feel your touch, and I want to touch you too.”

16
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:16,690
[GIVING SOME FEEDBACK.]
“I feel your touch, and I want to touch you too.”

17
00:01:16,690 --> 00:01:17,922
“I feel your touch, and I want to touch you too.”

18
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:20,570
[THE UMBRELLA GIRL LOOKS FAMILIAR.]

19
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:25,370
[SHE’S SENDING ‘NONG’ OFF TO SHOOT A SCENE.]

20
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:30,050
[REVIEW THE SCRIPT ONE LAST TIME.]

21
00:01:30,077 --> 00:01:31,878
Show your braid.

22
00:01:34,390 --> 00:01:35,983
If I didn’t have business to attend to soon,

23
00:01:36,474 --> 00:01:37,810
I’d drag you home with me.
[AND NOW THEY’RE FIGHTING.]

24
00:01:37,810 --> 00:01:39,210
[AND NOW THEY’RE FIGHTING.]

25
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:51,410
[WHAT ARE YOU TWO LOOKING AT?]

26
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:54,450
[REHEARSING, REHEARSING.]

27
00:02:09,040 --> 00:02:11,690
[BEING CLINGY AND SWEET.]

28
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:17,770
[TOO SWEET, COME ON!]

29
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:24,090
[TIME FOR SOME NICE PICS.]

30
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:26,210
[ARE YOU AFRAID SHE’LL DISAPPEAR?]

31
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:28,650
[GET-TOGETHER AROUND CAMPFIRE.]

32
00:02:31,388 --> 00:02:32,832
♪ You’re written in my heart ♪

33
00:02:32,983 --> 00:02:34,374
♪ No one knows but me ♪

34
00:02:35,082 --> 00:02:36,400
♪ The more I erase, the more I love you ♪

35
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:39,050
[THEY SEEM TO HAVE SO MUCH FUN.]
♪ The more I erase, the more I love you ♪

36
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,730
[LOOK AT THAT STUBBORN FACE.]

37
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:47,730
[A LITTLE MORE BRIEFING.]

38
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:58,410
[WHOSE HAIR IS IT?]

39
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:09,801
Pam, touch her to turn her face.

40
00:03:10,355 --> 00:03:11,124
Try it.
[LET’S TRY AGAIN.]

41
00:03:11,124 --> 00:03:13,120
Dokrak, turn away again.
[LET’S TRY AGAIN.]

42
00:03:14,730 --> 00:03:15,260
Yes.

43
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:21,250
[DROWSY, AREN’T YOU?]

44
00:03:23,110 --> 00:03:26,002
One step, two steps, then fall.

45
00:03:26,508 --> 00:03:27,702
One, two, fall.

46
00:03:28,398 --> 00:03:29,602
One, two, fall.
[ARRANGING THE FALL.]

47
00:03:31,014 --> 00:03:31,637
Try again.

48
00:03:31,971 --> 00:03:34,937
One, two. Oh, my gosh!

49
00:03:35,010 --> 00:03:36,165
Look at each other.
[THE DIRECTOR HELPS ENHANCE THE EMOTIONS.]

50
00:03:36,165 --> 00:03:36,570
[THE DIRECTOR HELPS ENHANCE THE EMOTIONS.]

51
00:03:36,590 --> 00:03:38,299
Okay.

52
00:03:38,382 --> 00:03:38,844
(Awesome!)

53
00:03:41,205 --> 00:03:42,711
And we’re done!

54
00:03:42,985 --> 00:03:43,625
Let me see.

55
00:03:47,826 --> 00:03:48,435
That’s it?

56
00:03:49,048 --> 00:03:50,754
It’s still the same. Nothing’s changed.

57
00:03:50,844 --> 00:03:51,389
Come on.

58
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:55,102
You wanted the same cut and same length,
[THE SAME CUT, AS YOU REQUESTED.]

59
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:57,714
so I only trimmed the edges.

60
00:04:01,552 --> 00:04:04,162
Doctor, why don’t you buy
some desserts for your son too?

61
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:06,832
[TALKING ABOUT HARD SELL.]

62
00:04:06,832 --> 00:04:08,010
And I’d like…
[TALKING ABOUT HARD SELL.]

63
00:04:09,068 --> 00:04:10,894
Oh, everything looks delicious.

64
00:04:11,059 --> 00:04:12,348
(How was that last scene?)

65
00:04:12,696 --> 00:04:14,968
It got easier, I would say.

66
00:04:15,432 --> 00:04:16,582
I remembered the dialogue,

67
00:04:16,660 --> 00:04:18,300
and I wasn’t that nervous
or put too much pressure on myself.

68
00:04:18,974 --> 00:04:19,800
Right, Grandma?

69
00:04:22,890 --> 00:04:25,866
(She suddenly talks to you,
so you lift your head in surprise.)

70
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:28,050
[REHEARSING TIME.]

71
00:04:28,050 --> 00:04:29,512
(Pam, hug her more tightly.)
[REHEARSING TIME.]

72
00:04:29,512 --> 00:04:29,970
[REHEARSING TIME.]

73
00:04:31,448 --> 00:04:34,022
After that, Pam grabs her hand.

74
00:04:34,047 --> 00:04:35,568
As if to say good night.

75
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:36,445
[ONCE AGAIN, THE BRIEF.]

76
00:04:36,445 --> 00:04:38,102
Don’t say it out loud. Think to yourself.
[ONCE AGAIN, THE BRIEF.]

77
00:04:38,102 --> 00:04:38,551
[ONCE AGAIN, THE BRIEF.]

78
00:04:38,561 --> 00:04:40,958
You can’t be loud, or your friend might wake up.

79
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,610
[LET’S GET SOME REST NOW.]

80
